<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Vingulmark</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Petty kingdom around the inner Oslofjord, a borderland between Norwegian and Danish power in the early Viking Age.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Vingulmark covered lands around the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslofjord">Oslofjord</a>, roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostfold">Østfold</a> and the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>. It is known from the sagas as one of the small kingdoms that the kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vestfold">Vestfold</a> sought to control in the 9th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The region was close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and was often under Danish influence, as was the whole area around the fjord called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viken">Viken</a>. Its people farmed the fertile lowlands and traded by sea. No reliable details of its rulers or laws survive.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The sagas say <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halfdan-the-black">Halfdan the Black</a> won Vingulmark and that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> held it as part of his realm. Danish kings continued to claim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viken">Viken</a> into the 11th century, but the district became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/vingulmark.jpg" alt="Vingulmark" width="320" height="497"><figcaption>Image: Ivar Refsdal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kart_over_Viken.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Vingulmark</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=815&amp;focus=vingulmark" aria-label="Vingulmark on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4905 169 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vingulmark lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5225 425L5225 425M5225 425L5274 535"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5225 425h0M5274 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5225 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5225 425h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=815&amp;focus=vingulmark">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
